{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_poison_pill_and_kill_poisonpill", "label": "PoisonPill", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/poison-pill-and-kill.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A user message, so it rides behind everything told earlier \u2014 the drain-before-stop guarantee. Anything told after it is not processed by this actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_poison_pill_and_kill_kill", "label": "Kill", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/poison-pill-and-kill.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raises ActorKilledError as if onReceive had thrown, so it goes through supervision \u2014 the only way for an outside actor to trip the supervision tree without modifying the supervised actor code. Under the default strategy it restarts rather than stops."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_poison_pill_and_kill_gracefulstop", "label": "gracefulStop(ref, timeoutMs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/poison-pill-and-kill.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A timeout is an outcome rather than an error, which is why it returns a boolean instead of rejecting; the budget is required because a default one would be the number that silently truncated somebody shutdown. On expiry it escalates so an impatient caller is not left with a live actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_poison_pill_and_kill_stopself", "label": "context.stopSelf", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/poison-pill-and-kill.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "